  "result": "Done. The bug was in the `removeMember` function at line 94 of `member-service.ts`. It was passing `\"owner\"` as the `nextRole` parameter to `assertLastOwnerRetained`, which caused the check to return early without validating anything. This allowed the last owner to be removed, leaving the organization with no owner.\n\nBy changing the parameter to `\"member\"`, the function now properly checks if the member being removed is currently an owner and if so, whether there are other owners to retain the invariant. This brings the removal path into alignment with the demotion path (which already had this check) and honors the documented contract that removal should be subject to the same last-owner rule as demotion.",
